From 0b5b5899e01e466b225747ab9966ab51b6f532a2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chiro <chiro2001@163.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 19:08:25 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 274/275] feat(avx512): native position-control plane
 (iota/compare/where, payload 8)

- add PXIO/PXCP/PXWH v1 descriptors with strict native decoding plus the
  FNV-1a descriptor tag shared with the verified SVE256 control wire
- bump artifact payload 7 -> 8 and native ABI marker :8 -> :9; the runtime
  decoder rejects a legacy host_reference-only payload without the wire
- record per-operation native/fallback tables with stable reasons; a plan is
  advertised native iff it has zero fallback entries
- native compare uses f32 and 64-bit signed/unsigned AVX-512 compares (bool
  lanes truthify like the host); native where uses _mm512_mask_blend_ps /
  _mm512_mask_blend_epi64 and quiet-NaN semantics that match the host
  Python-float round trip; native iota uses exact __int128 arithmetic
- plan_execution reports python_list_elements=0 for the native plane and the
  fallback reason for explicit host paths
- tests: differential matrices (NaN/sNaN payloads, subnormals, extremes,
  broadcast, scalar operands), metadata audit, payload/descriptor tampering,
  baseline cross-tree bitwise comparison and UNGATED local timing

(cherry picked from commit 8dedc590995aeb72cf51e763f9e0fa12ad59503f)
